IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `Trust Freedom card — Trust Miles: how they are earned and converted`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENTS. Two web pages of Trust Bank Singapore Limited, both held by
-- clause-text digest (registers/source-bundle.json):
--   trust-freedom-miles-page   the Freedom credit card Miles product page.
--       A MARKETING STATEMENT, not terms and conditions. It is the only held
--       place that states the ongoing earn rate: "Earn 1.3 Trust Miles per
--       S$1 on local and foreign spends (awarded for every S$5 spent), which
--       you can convert instantly to Max Miles or KrisFlyer Miles at 1:1
--       ratio." It also says "No FX Fees" and "No annual card fee".
--   heymax-trust-welcome-bonus-tnc  HeyMax's terms for the Max Miles codes of the
--       launch welcome bonus (see trust-spend-and-get.l4). Its cl.2.6 lists the
--       excluded merchant category codes and says the list "also applies to Trust
--       Freedom Card ongoing rewards". That sentence is the only held statement
--       that any category is excluded from the ongoing earn, and it is HeyMax's
--       sentence about Trust's list, not Trust's own.
--   trust-miles-redemption-tnc  "Last updated on: 21 September 2026, Version:
--       1". States the CONVERSION of Trust Miles (to HeyMax Max Miles and
--       Singapore Airlines KrisFlyer miles, 1 Trust mile = 1 partner mile),
--       a conversion fee of $27.25 (inclusive of GST) per transfer, and that
--       a reversed transaction can be corrected by debiting Trust Miles. It
--       does not state how Trust Miles are earned.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT HELD, AND WHAT THE MODULE DOES ABOUT IT.
-- (1) The Freedom card's own terms and conditions, and the "Trust / NTUC Link
--     credit card product terms" that the Spend & Get promotion cites for what
--     is ineligible, are not held. So WHAT SPEND EARNS is stated only by the
--     product page's "local and foreign spends", and every answer names the
--     condition "the issuer's own product terms, which are not held, may
--     exclude this spend". A charge kind the page does not mention is given a
--     floor of 0 and a ceiling of the full earn.
-- (1a) THE FORK F-trust-ongoing-exclusions. The product page excludes nothing
--     ("local and foreign spends"); HeyMax cl.2.6 says a list of 32 MCCs does not
--     earn the ongoing rewards. The two cannot both be applied: the page is the
--     issuer's and says nothing is excluded, HeyMax is not the issuer and says
--     these are. The module does not choose. A purchase at a listed code has a
--     floor of 0 (HeyMax) and a ceiling of the full earn (the page), and names
--     the open reading; a purchase at an unlisted code is unaffected.
-- (2) The page says "awarded for every S$5 spent" and gives 1.3 per S$1, i.e.
--     6.5 Trust Miles per complete S$5. It states no rounding of the 0.5 mile;
--     the module does not round, and "for every S$5 spent" is the page's own
--     wording.
-- (3) The reward choice. The Spend & Get terms speak of customers who
--     "selected Miles as your reward type"; the page is the Miles page. A
--     cardholder whose reward choice is Cashback or Stockback earns something
--     else, which no held document states, so the module answers 0 Trust Miles
--     for her and says so.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `The earn`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Trust Miles per S$1 on local and foreign spend` MEANS 1.3

-- "(awarded for every S$5 spent)": the earn runs in complete S$5 blocks.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the size of a Trust Miles block in S$` MEANS 5

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Trust Miles earned on` amount MEANS
    (FLOOR (amount DIVIDED BY `the size of a Trust Miles block in S$`)) TIMES (`the size of a Trust Miles block in S$` TIMES `Trust Miles per S$1 on local and foreign spend`)

-- The page's "No FX Fees": the foreign transaction fee rate.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Trust foreign transaction fee rate` MEANS 0


§§ `The conversion (redemption terms)`

-- "1 Trust mile = 1 Max mile", "1 Trust mile = 1 KrisFlyer mile"; minimum
-- partner miles to transfer 1; "Conversion fee per transfer $27.25 (inclusive
-- of GST)", charged to the Freedom card on a successful conversion.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`partner miles per Trust Mile` MEANS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Trust conversion fee per transfer in S$` MEANS 27.25

-- What a conversion of this many Trust Miles costs per partner mile, in S$:
-- the fee is flat, so the cost per mile falls as the batch grows.
GIVEN trustMilesConverted IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the conversion fee per partner mile for` trustMilesConverted MEANS
    IF trustMilesConverted AT LEAST 1
    THEN `the Trust conversion fee per transfer in S$` DIVIDED BY (trustMilesConverted TIMES `partner miles per Trust Mile`)
    ELSE 0


§§ `The merchant category codes HeyMax says are excluded`

-- HeyMax cl.2.6: 4900, 6513, 7349 (utilities, rentals and cleaning services);
-- 4829, 5960, 6010, 6011, 6012, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6540 (financial institutions,
-- securities brokers, quasi cash, insurance, stored value card purchase or load,
-- and wire transfer); 7995 (gambling); 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299
-- (educational institutions); 8398, 8651, 8661, 9211, 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399,
-- 9402, 9405 (charitable services, political organisations, religious
-- organisations and government payments); and 7299, 7399, 8999 (other services).
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Trust excluded category codes per HeyMax` MEANS
    LIST 4900, 6513, 7349, 4829, 5960, 6010, 6011, 6012, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6540,
         7995, 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299, 8398, 8651, 8661, 9211, 9222,
         9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405, 7299, 7399, 8999


§§ `The answer for one purchase`

GIVEN h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Trust holder chose Miles` h MEANS
    h's `reward choice` EQUALS `Miles`

-- The only charge kind the page's "local and foreign spends" plainly covers is
-- an ordinary retail purchase. A reversed charge earns nothing (redemption
-- terms 9).
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Trust page plainly covers` p MEANS
    p's `charge kind` EQUALS `Retail purchase` AND NOT (p's `later reversed`)

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Trust Freedom answer when the code is settled` p h MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Trust holder chose Miles` h)
            THEN `nothing is earned on` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Trust Miles` `per` "Trust Freedom Miles page: the Miles reward choice"
        IF p's `later reversed`
            THEN `nothing is earned on` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Trust Miles` `per` "Trust Miles redemption terms 9: reversed transactions"
        OTHERWISE `an answer for` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Trust Miles` `of` (`trust floor` p) `to` (`the Trust Miles earned on` (p's `amount in SGD`)) `wanting` 0 `at` (JUST `partner miles per Trust Mile`) `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `No pot` `depending on` (LIST `The issuer's own product terms, which are not held, may exclude this spend`) `per` "Trust Freedom Miles page (marketing); redemption terms (conversion)"

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Trust Freedom answer for a code HeyMax lists` p h MEANS
    `bracketed from` (`nothing is earned on` `Trust Freedom` `in` `Trust Miles` `per` "HeyMax welcome-bonus terms cl.2.6: the excluded-MCC list 'also applies to Trust Freedom Card ongoing rewards'") `to` (`Trust Freedom answer when the code is settled` p h) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, h IS A `Trust holder`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Trust Freedom earns on` p h MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the code is unknown for` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`Trust Freedom answer for a code HeyMax lists` p h) `to` (`Trust Freedom answer when the code is settled` p h) `adding` (LIST `The merchant category code is not known`)
        IF `the code is among` p `the Trust excluded category codes per HeyMax`
            THEN `Trust Freedom answer for a code HeyMax lists` p h
        OTHERWISE `Trust Freedom answer when the code is settled` p h

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`trust floor` p MEANS
    IF `the Trust page plainly covers` p
    THEN `the Trust Miles earned on` (p's `amount in SGD`)
    ELSE 0


§§ `Illustrations`

`a Trust holder who chose Miles` MEANS `Trust holder` WITH
    `reward choice`                  IS `Miles`
    `new Trust credit card customer` IS TRUE
    `card approved on`               IS Date 22 9 2026
    `Quest spend tiers in S$`        IS LIST 1000, 5000, 15000

`a Trust holder who chose Cashback` MEANS `Trust holder` WITH
    `reward choice`                  IS `Cashback`
    `new Trust credit card customer` IS TRUE
    `card approved on`               IS Date 22 9 2026
    `Quest spend tiers in S$`        IS LIST 1000, 5000, 15000

`a Trust purchase of S$100` MEANS `the base purchase`
`a Trust purchase of S$100 in another currency` MEANS `purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Another foreign currency`
`a Trust purchase of S$4.99` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 4.99
`a Trust purchase of S$9.99` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 9.99
`a Trust purchase of S$12` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 12

-- The page: 1.3 per S$1, awarded for every S$5: S$100 earns 130.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$100` `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 130
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$100` `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 130

-- "local and foreign spends" alike: a foreign-currency charge earns the same, and the fee rate is 0.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$100 in another currency` `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 130
#ASSERT `Trust foreign transaction fee rate` EQUALS 0

-- "Awarded for every S$5 spent": under S$5 earns nothing; S$9.99 earns as S$5; S$12 earns as S$10.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$4.99` `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$9.99` `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 6.5
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$12` `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 13

-- Another reward choice earns no Trust Miles.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$100` `a Trust holder who chose Cashback`)'s excluded

-- A reversed charge earns nothing.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` (`purchase later reversed` `a Trust purchase of S$100`) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s excluded

-- A charge kind the page does not plainly cover has a floor of 0 and a full ceiling.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` (`purchase of kind` `a Trust purchase of S$100` `Bill payment`) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` (`purchase of kind` `a Trust purchase of S$100` `Bill payment`) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 130

-- Every answer names the unheld terms.
#ASSERT elem `The issuer's own product terms, which are not held, may exclude this spend` ((`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$100` `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `depends on`)

-- Conversion: 1:1 into partner miles, so miles equal Trust Miles.
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`Trust Freedom earns on` `a Trust purchase of S$100` `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 130

-- The fee is flat: converting 1,000 Trust Miles costs S$0.02725 a mile; 100 costs S$0.2725 a mile; none costs nothing.
#ASSERT `the conversion fee per partner mile for` 1000 EQUALS 0.02725
#ASSERT `the conversion fee per partner mile for` 100 EQUALS 0.2725
#ASSERT `the conversion fee per partner mile for` 0 EQUALS 0

-- F-trust-ongoing-exclusions: a code on HeyMax's list has a floor of 0 and the page's full earn as ceiling.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` (`recoded purchase` `a Trust purchase of S$100` 4900) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` (`recoded purchase` `a Trust purchase of S$100` 4900) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 130
#ASSERT elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`Trust Freedom earns on` (`recoded purchase` `a Trust purchase of S$100` 7399) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `depends on`)
-- ... a hospital (8062) is on neither list: the page's earn stands.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` (`recoded purchase` `a Trust purchase of S$100` 8062) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 130
#ASSERT NOT (elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`Trust Freedom earns on` (`recoded purchase` `a Trust purchase of S$100` 8062) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `depends on`))
-- ... the code not known: floor 0, ceiling 130.
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` (`purchase with unknown code` `a Trust purchase of S$100`) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`Trust Freedom earns on` (`purchase with unknown code` `a Trust purchase of S$100`) `a Trust holder who chose Miles`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 130
#ASSERT count `the Trust excluded category codes per HeyMax` EQUALS 32
